Restart machines through their management controllers. --name takes a comma-separated list, and the command applies to every listed machine at once. Success reports the power state the controller proved, not the state that was requested.

Usage:
  bootwright machine restart [flags]

Examples:
  bootwright machine restart --context lab --name node

Flags:
      --force           Cut power instead of asking the operating system to shut down
      --name string     Select comma-separated machine names (required)
      --output string   Select output mode (values: text, json) (default "text")
      --yes             Confirm the command's ordinary confirmation

Global Flags:
      --context string             Select a context (default: current context)
  -h, --help                       Show help for this command
      --ssh-ask-sudo-password      Request the borrowed account's sudo password
      --ssh-id-file string         Offer an explicit private key for eligible SSH access
      --ssh-user string            Borrow an explicit POSIX account for eligible SSH access
      --ssh-user-for-provisioned   Extend the borrowed account to provisioned machines
